                        <!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p class="mb-3">The <code>dotkernel/dot-maker</code> library, also named DotMaker, is designed to <strong>programmatically generate project files and directories</strong> that match the Dotkernel file structure inspired by Mezzio.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p class="mb-3">Handling the file creation and configuration task manually invites mistakes that nobody has time for. Enter DotMaker which provides a big <strong>productivity boost</strong> compared to doing everything manually by promoting <strong>consistenty and standardization</strong> for these common tasks.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p class="mb-3">DotMaker is inspired by <a href="https://github.com/symfony/maker-bundle" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Symfony Maker Bundle</a> in terms of functionality. Mezzio has its own <a href="https://docs.mezzio.dev/mezzio/v3/reference/cli-tooling/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">CLI Tooling</a> that performs similar actions, while DotMaker has a more opinionated naming pattern and is designed specifically for Dotkernel applications.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:embed {"url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CPDilXP2kAc","type":"video","providerNameSlug":"youtube","responsive":true,"className":"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"} -->
